\p{\strong{Useful note.} If #{\ker\Phi = \lbrace e\rbrace } then #{G} is isomorphic to a subgroup of #{\mathrm{Sym}(X)}; we write #{G \lesssim \mathrm{Sym}(X)}. So if #{|G|} does not divide #{|\mathrm{Sym}(X)|} then #{\ker\Phi \neq \lbrace e\rbrace }.}

